\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I am not skilled to understand
\par What God hath willed, what
\par God hath planned;
\par I only know at His right hand
\par Stands One who is my Saviour.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I take God at His word and deed:
\par Christ died to save me, this I read;
\par And in my heart I find a need
\par Of Him to be my Saviour.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And was there then no other way
\par For God to take? I cannot say,
\par I only bless Him, day by day,
\par Who saved me through my Saviour.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 4. That He should leave His place on high
\par And come for sinful man to die,
\par You count it strange? So do not I,
\par Since I have known my Saviour.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. And O that He fulfilled may see
\par The travail of His soul in me,
\par And with His work contented be,
\par As I with my dear Saviour!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Yea, living, dying, let me bring
\par My strength, my solace, from this spring,
\par That He who lives to be my King
\par Once died to be my Saviour.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

